{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLgu5YUCZXMm1yKPfa5G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: nested compound models now get the correct separability matrix.\n\n**Cause:** In `_cstack` in `astropy/modeling/separable.py`, when the right-hand side of `&` was already a compound model, its separability matrix was replaced with a block of all `1`s. That wiped out its internal structure and made every one of its inputs look tied to every output.\n\n**Fix:** I changed one line (line 245) so the right operand's real matrix is copied in:\n\n```python\ncright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = right\n```\n\n**Verification:** `separability_matrix(m.Pix2Sky_TAN() & (m.Linear1D(10) & m.Linear1D(5)))` now returns the expected block-diagonal matrix, and all 11 tests in `astropy/modeling/tests/test_separable.py` pass.\n\nThe tests wouldn't run with the command you gave in this environment, so I used `-p no:astropy_header -W ignore::DeprecationWarning`. The first flag gets around an import error in the `pytest_astropy_header` plugin; the second stops a distutils deprecation warning from being treated as an error."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":176,"cache_read_input_tokens":20132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":176},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ea037c8-c375-4716-981a-89ae3e5bf249","uuid":"df18f43b-74f0-4d07-a572-99b5f33ae081","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:58:55.879Z","request_id":"req_011ChLgu5NZgHJBhppEAuu7i"}
